From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ole Algoritme <olealgoritme@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 12:08:25 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] nvk: VK_NV_framebuffer_mixed_samples, rasterization at more
 samples than the color attachments

Direct2D fills anti-aliased paths (the Windows 11 shell's vector icons,
complex geometry) with D3D11.1 target-independent rasterization:
ForcedSampleCount 16 in the rasterizer state with a single-sample render
target, and a pixel shader that takes its alpha from the number of
covered samples in SV_Coverage divided by 16.  Vulkan can only express
that with mixed samples (rasterizationSamples 16, color attachment 1
sample); without it DXVK rasterizes at the attachment's single sample,
the coverage has one bit, and every covered pixel gets 1/16 of its alpha
(a Direct2D test fill: maximum alpha 16 instead of 255).

The hardware has done this since Maxwell B: SET_TIR RASTER_N_TARGET_M
with SET_ANTI_ALIAS_RASTER giving the raster sample count, next to
SET_ANTI_ALIAS for the attachments.  VK_NV_framebuffer_mixed_samples
(Maxwell B+):

- nvk_flush_mixed_samples(), when the rasterization samples or the
  coverage modulation mode change (every render pass begin dirties the
  former): rasterizationSamples above the color attachments' count, with
  no depth/stencil attachment, turns target-independent rasterization on
  with that raster sample count, and off otherwise.  The pixel shader's
  covmask then has one bit per raster sample; without sample shading NAK
  hands it to gl_SampleMaskIn as is.
- The color and depth/stencil sample counts are tracked separately
  (nvk_rendering_state::color_samples, zs_samples), in render passes and
  in secondaries, whose inheritance may give them with
  VkAttachmentSampleCountInfoAMD.  The hardware has one sample layout for
  color and Z (SET_ANTI_ALIAS) and raster samples above it, not a Z
  buffer at the raster count, so a depth/stencil attachment is not part
  of target-independent rasterization: with one bound the draw
  rasterizes at the attachments' count, and a depth/stencil attachment
  with more samples than the color attachments (which the extension
  allows) is not supported; color and Z then use the color layout, which
  keeps every access inside both images.  D3D11 forbids depth-stencil
  views with a forced sample count, and DXVK never mixes them.
- CLEAR_SURFACE with target-independent rasterization on is a class
  error (GB202: Xid 69, CLEAR_SURFACE 0x19d0, error code 0x124), so it
  is turned off at every render pass begin (before SET_ANTI_ALIAS and
  the load-op clears), before vkCmdClearAttachments and before
  STORE_ZCULL; the next draw that wants it turns it back on.  A CPU flag
  (on at command buffer begin and after secondaries) keeps the off
  method to once.
- At queue init: off, coverage reduced to the color samples by the
  affinity map (the extension's merge reduction), alpha to coverage and
  the occlusion sample count on the raster samples (the spec orders
  multisample coverage and sample counting before coverage reduction).
- Coverage modulation (VkPipelineCoverageModulationStateCreateInfoNV):
  SET_TIR_MODULATION component select with the linear function.  A
  modulation table is modulated linearly: the hardware's coefficient
  table took a class error on GB202 (Xid 69, error code 4) with a valid
  table, and its indexing for raster/color ratios below 16 could not be
  verified.  The extended dynamic state 3 coverage modulation states stay
  unadvertised.
- The shader-visible sample positions (root table) grow to 16 entries,
  all of a 16-sample raster: D3D11 pull-model interpolation
  (EvaluateAttributeAtSample) can name indices 8 to 15 under
  target-independent rasterization.  interpolateAtSample loads the
  position byte by index.  The root table layout after the draw
  parameters is unchanged.
- SET_ANTI_ALIAS 4X4 (16 samples, only ever rasterized without
  attachments) gets single-pass sample masks instead of reaching
  UNREACHABLE.

The extension requires sampleShadingEnable = VK_FALSE with mixed
samples, so the per-pass sample masks stay as they are.  A device
without the extension enabled emits nothing new.

Verified on an RTX 5090 (GB202) with guest/nvk-rm/tests/
vk_mixed_samples_test.c (raster 2, 4, 8 and 16 to one color sample,
without and with linear modulation, a secondary, a depth attachment) and
guest/windows/tools/d2d_tir_probe.cpp through DXVK.
